@startuml

<style>
.OS {
    LineThickness 5.0
}
</style>

skinparam sequenceArrowColor Black
skinparam sequenceParticipantBackgroundColor White
skinparam sequenceParticipantBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceLifeLineBorderColor Black
skinparam sequenceGroupBorderColor DarkGray
skinparam sequenceGroupBodyBackgroundColor #FAFAFA
skinparam NoteBackgroundColor LightYellow
skinparam NoteBorderColor Gray
skinparam NoteTextAlignment left
skinparam ParticipantFontName Courier
skinparam sequenceFontName Courier
skinparam ArrowFontName Courier

title Server <-> Client Sequence Diagram: Underlying-Layer (OS/Transport) Faults

note over client_app, server_app
  Companion to server_client_sequence.puml (happy path) and
  server_client_internal_fault_sequence.puml (library-internal resource limits).
  This diagram covers faults originating in the OS/transport layer that the
  library detects and reports, but does not itself cause or prevent -
  i.e. non-happy paths of the underlying layers, not user contract misuse
  and not library-internal bookkeeping limits.
end note

participant "ClientApp" as client_app
participant "IClientConnection" as client_conn
participant "IPC Mechanism"  as os <<OS>>
participant "IServerConnection" as server_conn
participant "IServer" as server
participant "ServerApp" as server_app

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Connection Refused: Insufficient Permissions (StopReason::kPermission) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

client_app -> client_conn : IClientConnection::Start(\n  state_callback,\n  notify_callback\n)
client_conn -> client_app : state_callback(kStarting)
client_conn -> os : [IPC] connect attempt
os -> client_conn : [IPC] connection refused (EACCES-equivalent)
client_conn -> client_app : state_callback(kStopping)
client_conn -> client_app : state_callback(kStopped)
note left
  GetStopReason() == StopReason::kPermission
  Per i_client_connection.h: "highly unlikely to
  have a successful Restart()" for this reason
end note

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Server Bind/Startup Failure ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

server_app -> server : IServerFactory::Create(\n  protocol_config,\n  server_config\n)
server -> os : IServer::StartListening(...)
os -> server : [IPC] bind/listen fails\n(e.g. service identifier already in use,\nresource limits reached)
server --> server_app : score::cpp::expected_blank<Error>\n(error)
note right
  IServer::StartListening() returning an error is
  the only signal; the server never starts accepting
  connections. Grounds the previously un-evidenced FTA
  basic events "Duplicate Server Name" and "Server
  factory queue size configured below the required
  minimum" (fta_ipc_channel_unavailable.puml, IE_Startup).
end note

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Peer Crash / Unexpected Disconnect While Ready (StopReason::kClosedByPeer) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

note over client_app, server_app
  Setup and connection establishment already completed as in
  server_client_sequence.puml (omitted here for brevity); both
  endpoints are in their Ready-equivalent state.
end note

server_app -> server_conn : (server process crashes / exits)
os -> client_conn : [IPC] peer closed / broken pipe detected
client_conn -> client_app : state_callback(kStopping)
client_conn -> client_app : state_callback(kStopped)
note left : GetStopReason() == StopReason::kClosedByPeer

os -> server_conn : [IPC] peer closed
note right : Detected independently on the
server side once the OS reports the peer gone
server_conn -> server_app : DisconnectCallback(connection)\nor IConnectionHandler::OnDisconnect(connection)
destroy server_conn

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Communication Error Prevents Continuation (StopReason::kIoError) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

client_app -> client_conn : Send(message) / SendWaitReply(...) / SendWithCallback(...)
client_conn -> os : [IPC] SEND/REQUEST
os -> client_conn : [IPC] transport error\n(e.g. corrupted framing, unexpected errno)
client_conn -> client_app : state_callback(kStopping)
client_conn -> client_app : state_callback(kStopped)
note left : GetStopReason() == StopReason::kIoError

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== SendWithCallback: Reply Lost Because Peer Disconnects Mid-Flight ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

client_app -> client_conn : SendWithCallback(message, reply_callback)
client_conn -> os : [IPC] REQUEST message
os -> server_conn : [IPC] REQUEST message
server_conn -> server : IConnectionHandler::OnMessageSentWithReply(\n  connection, message\n)
server_app -> server_conn : (server disconnects/crashes\nbefore calling Reply())
client_conn -> client_app : reply_callback(error)
note left
  Per i_client_connection.h: "if the server receives
  the message but dies or disconnects before the reply
  arrives to the client, the error will be passed to
  the callback; the method itself will not return
  an error."
end note

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== System-Wide Memory Exhaustion (ENOMEM) ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

client_app -> client_conn : Start(...) / Send(...)
client_conn -> os : [IPC] connect / send attempt
os -> client_conn : ENOMEM (system memory allocation limit reached)
note left
  Per client-server.md: "We don't expect to be able to
  preallocate all the needed system memory resources.
  We rely on ENOMEM error for handling of system memory
  allocation limits on QNX." Not preventable by the
  library; reported the same way as other transport
  errors (kIoError or a Send()/SendWaitReply() error).
end note

' -----------------------------------------------------------------
== Server-Side Incoming Backpressure Delegated to the OS ==
' -----------------------------------------------------------------

client_app -> client_conn : Send(message) [rapid, repeated]
client_conn -> os : [IPC] SEND message
note over os
  Today, neither UnixDomainServer nor QnxDispatchServer
  implements ServerConfig::max_queued_sends as an
  internal ring buffer (see memory_and_size_limits_findings.md,
  finding 4). Backpressure for incoming Send/REQUEST
  messages is delegated entirely to the OS socket/channel
  buffer, not to library-managed queueing.
end note
os -> server_conn : [IPC] SEND message (buffered by OS)
note right
  If the OS-level buffer is full, the OS-level send call
  on the client side blocks or fails (EAGAIN-equivalent)
  before the message is considered sent by the library -
  i.e. this is an OS-layer fault, not the
  library-internal, deterministic rejection shown for
  max_queued_sends/max_async_replies in
  server_client_internal_fault_sequence.puml.
end note

@enduml
